01:39:35,440 --> 01:39:41,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Anyway, sa ating Secretary, magaling at masipag.

2621
01:39:41,440 --> 01:39:45,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: I can vouch for him na masipag talaga yan na Secretary.

2622
01:39:45,440 --> 01:39:46,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At alam niyo po yan.

2623
01:39:46,440 --> 01:39:50,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: And to the entire DOLE family, good day to all.

2624
01:39:50,440 --> 01:40:01,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Allow me to deliver a manifestation regarding the proposed budgets of the DOLE, Department of Labor and Employment and its attached agencies and corporations.

2625
01:40:01,440 --> 01:40:04,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Gusto ko lang lang pong batiin lahat.

2626
01:40:04,440 --> 01:40:15,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Institute for Labor Studies, ILS, National Conciliation and Mediation Board, NCMB, National Labor Relations Commission, NLRC. Ma'am.

2627
01:40:15,440 --> 01:40:28,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: National Wages and Productivity Commission, NWPC, and PRC, Professional Regulation Commission. Ma'am.

2628
01:40:28,440 --> 01:40:33,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Occupational Safety and Health Center, Employees Compensation Commission.

2629
01:40:33,440 --> 01:40:36,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sa lahat po ng attached agencies, magandang hapon po sa inyong lahat.

2630
01:40:36,440 --> 01:40:38,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At salamat po sa inyong servisyo.

2631
01:40:38,440 --> 01:40:43,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Mr. Chair, for 2027, the proposed expenditure program of DOLE is 47.

2632
01:40:43,440 --> 01:40:59,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: 47.726 billion equivalent to only 0.66 of the 7.2 trillion total national expenditure program.

2633
01:40:59,440 --> 01:41:04,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sobrang liit po ng share ng DOLE sa kabuhang national budget ngayong taong ito.

2634
01:41:04,440 --> 01:41:10,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kung baga sa cake, icing lang po ito. Napaka-liit.

2635
01:41:10,440 --> 01:41:12,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Mr. Chair,

2636
01:41:13,440 --> 01:41:17,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: May steadfast advocate for the welfare of every Filipino worker.

2637
01:41:17,440 --> 01:41:28,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: I support the department in fulfilling its mandate to protect the rights, promote the welfare, and improve the working conditions of our labor force.

2638
01:41:28,440 --> 01:41:32,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: May katanungan lang po ako, Mr. Chair, sa ating sekretary.

2639
01:41:32,440 --> 01:41:41,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: I would like to commend the department for its recent wage order under which minimum wage earners in the National Capital Region

2640
01:41:41,440 --> 01:41:46,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: will receive a 60 peso daily wage increase.

2641
01:41:46,440 --> 01:41:52,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ito po yung naging controversial nung mga nakarang buwan, nakarang araw.

2642
01:41:52,440 --> 01:41:58,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Dagdag tulong po ito sa mahigit 1.1 million minimum wage earners in Metro Manila.

2643
01:41:58,440 --> 01:42:08,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: I hope that the department will continue to monitor compliance with the wage order and provide guidance to both workers and employers on its proper implementation.

2644
01:42:08,440 --> 01:42:13,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: We also hope that the circumstances that previously resulted in a delayed

2645
01:42:13,440 --> 01:42:21,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: the implementation of the wage increase will not happen again so that the benefits intended for our workers will not be further delayed.

2646
01:42:21,440 --> 01:42:29,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At bawat piso, bawat sentimo po, lalong-lalo na po sa mga ordinaryong manggagawa ay napakahalaga po sa kanila.

2647
01:42:29,440 --> 01:42:32,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Lalong-lalo na po sa mga isang kahig, isang tuka nating kababayan.

2648
01:42:32,440 --> 01:42:36,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Yun po ang unahin natin na bigyan ng konsiderasyon at priority.

2649
01:42:36,440 --> 01:42:44,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At sana rin po, hindi lamang Metro Manila ang ating pagtuunan ng pansin, tingnan rin po natin ang kalagayan ng mga manggagawa sa iba't ibang regyon,

2650
01:42:44,440 --> 01:42:49,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: lalo na sa mga lugar kung saan mas marami ang nangangailangan ng dagdag na suporta.

2651
01:42:49,440 --> 01:42:57,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: We hope that the department can take a more encompassing approach in addressing wage concerns

2652
01:42:57,440 --> 01:43:05,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: so that more Filipino workers wherever they may be in the country can benefit from meaningful wage increases and better economic opportunities.

2653
01:43:05,440 --> 01:43:10,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Alam niyo po, Mr. Chair, matagal na po ang panawagan ng mga Pilipino ang pagtaas ng minimum wage sa bansa.

2654
01:43:10,440 --> 01:43:22,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Patuloy ang pagtaas ng presyo ng mga bilihin dahil mas mabilis pa ang pagtataas ng bilihin kaysa sa pagtataas ng sahod.

2655
01:43:22,440 --> 01:43:30,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Masasabi natin na mismatch pa rin ang pagitan ng sahod at presyo ng bilihin at mababa pa rin ang purchasing power ng ating mga kababayan.

2656
01:43:30,440 --> 01:43:34,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kaya naman, inihihain rin po natin dito sa Senado, itong Senate Bill number 8.

2657
01:43:35,440 --> 01:43:55,120
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: 175 na naglalayong magbibigay ng dagdag 100 peso sa daily minimum wage across the board para matulungan ang mga magagawa na makasabay sa patuloy na pagtaas ng presyo ng pangunahing bilihin at masiguro ang disenteng pamumuhay para sa kanilang pamilya.

2658
01:43:55,120 --> 01:44:11,220
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At parate ko nga sinasabi sa mga malalaking negosyante, kung malaki naman po ang inyong kita, kung di naman po masakit sa inyo, sana po ipamahagin nyo na lang po ito, lalong-lalo na po sa mga maliliit na magagawa na isang kahig, isang tuka lang po ang kanilang kinikita.

2659
01:44:12,480 --> 01:44:20,920
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Mr. Chair, may I ask the good secretary, the Regional Tripartite Wages and Productivity Board for the National Capital Region,

2660
01:44:21,560 --> 01:44:25,100
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: granted an 85 daily minimum wage increase to be implemented.

2661
01:44:25,120 --> 01:44:39,200
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ito yung naka-TRO. At kung tutusin, 85 na nga lang po ito, mas mababa pa kumpara sa isinasulong nating 100 peso wage increase. Ano na bang nangyari dito? At ano ang update nito, Mr. Secretary?

2662
01:44:40,100 --> 01:44:41,700
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yes, Secretary T. Lentino.

2663
01:44:42,180 --> 01:44:44,720
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Salamat po, Mr. Chair, Senator Bongo.

2664
01:44:45,360 --> 01:44:53,680
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Pagaya po nung nabanggit nyo, kasama nyo po ako sa pagsusulong ng mas mataas na sahod para sa ating manggagawa.

2665
01:44:54,040 --> 01:44:55,000
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Pumerma din po ako.

2666
01:44:55,120 --> 01:44:59,480
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Nandito pa ako doon sa 100 peso increase noong 19 Congress.

2667
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,740
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Tungkol po sa status ng Wage Order No. 27, meron po itong kinakaharap na limang kaso.

2668
01:45:07,700 --> 01:45:17,060
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yung isang kaso po ay sa Branch 152 ng PASIG kung saan merong na-issue yung status quo order,

2669
01:45:17,920 --> 01:45:21,440
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: tapos yung pasunod, TRO, tapos injunction.

2670
01:45:21,440 --> 01:45:31,100
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Pangalawang kaso po ay nasa Nabotas RTC at ang dalawang kaso po na meron po dalawang kaso nakasampang ngayon

2671
01:45:31,100 --> 01:45:32,780
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: pending sa Court of Appeals.

2672
01:45:33,480 --> 01:45:40,520
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yung isa po ang nag-file ay isang employer at yung isa kung hindi ako nagkakamali ay employees group naman.

2673
01:45:41,380 --> 01:45:44,000
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Meron din po isang nakabimbi na kaso sa Supreme Court.

2674
01:45:44,660 --> 01:45:51,080
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Lahat po ito ay hindi po namin alam kung kailan matatapos isa-isa.

2675
01:45:51,440 --> 01:45:54,600
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kaya ano pa? Dalawa po ang hindi namin alam.

2676
01:45:55,180 --> 01:45:57,280
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Hindi namin alam kung kailan matatapos.

2677
01:45:57,980 --> 01:46:00,540
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Pangalawa, hindi namin alam kung ano magiging risulta.

2678
01:46:01,360 --> 01:46:10,180
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kung ito ba ay magiging pabor o hindi pabor o magtatagal hanggang Disyembre o 2027.

2679
01:46:10,180 --> 01:46:16,880
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kaya nga po, Your Honor, minarapat namin, bagamat hindi pa bahagi ng inyong tanong,

2680
01:46:17,500 --> 01:46:21,220
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: na minarapat ng Wage Board na isulong.

2681
01:46:21,440 --> 01:46:26,100
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At dumaan sa prosesong tama sa ngayon sa batas, yung Wage Order 28.

2682
01:46:27,000 --> 01:46:37,340
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yung Wage Order 28 ay 60 pesos na implemented noong September 26, 2026, noong nakaraan linggo.

2683
01:46:37,880 --> 01:46:42,920
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang tanong po ng marami at siguro baka bumabagabag din sa kaisipan ng iba,

2684
01:46:43,700 --> 01:46:48,200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: e ba ano pa, paano mangyayari doon sa 85 at doon sa bagong 60?

2685
01:46:48,200 --> 01:46:51,020
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang dapat po siguro nating isipin,

2686
01:46:51,440 --> 01:47:00,540
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ay yung Wage Order 28 ay pumatong at nagsimula doon sa Wage Order 26

2687
01:47:00,540 --> 01:47:06,220
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: na umiiral bago i-implement si 28.

2688
01:47:06,580 --> 01:47:09,520
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yun po yung umiiral before September 26.

2689
01:47:09,720 --> 01:47:12,680
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, yung mga nagtatanong bakit bumaba, wala pong binaba.

2690
01:47:13,160 --> 01:47:16,840
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kasi yung umpong 26 ang umiiral.

2691
01:47:16,840 --> 01:47:20,220
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, from 26 na 695 pesos,

2692
01:47:20,220 --> 01:47:25,540
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: napadagdag po yung 60 pesos ay yung po ay naging 755.

2693
01:47:25,860 --> 01:47:33,160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Dahil si 27 ay nakakahon po sa husgado na hindi natin alam kung kailan matatapos

2694
01:47:33,160 --> 01:47:36,520
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: at ano po yung magiging risulta.

2695
01:47:36,700 --> 01:47:43,000
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kaya may narapat po sa ngayon din sa batas na ipasa yung Wage Order 27 ng Wage Board

2696
01:47:43,000 --> 01:47:48,460
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: at ito po ay kinatigan in a firm ng National Wages and Productivity Commission.

2697
01:47:48,460 --> 01:47:50,180
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At simula nga noong September,

2698
01:47:50,220 --> 01:47:51,680
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: 26 ay umiiral na.

2699
01:47:52,180 --> 01:47:56,060
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, ito pong ngayong araw pong ngayon ay at renta,

2700
01:47:56,180 --> 01:48:03,720
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: dapat po yung 26, 27, 26, 28, 29, 30,

2701
01:48:03,900 --> 01:48:09,920
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: halos apat na araw ay kasama na po dapat sa pay slip ng ating mga minimum wage earners.

2702
01:48:10,040 --> 01:48:14,000
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At pagdating po ng 15 ay kasama na rin talaga dapat.

2703
01:48:14,000 --> 01:48:15,100
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So, 60 pesos po.

2704
01:48:15,140 --> 01:48:15,960
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: 60 pesos po.

2705
01:48:16,680 --> 01:48:18,240
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Dito sa Metro Manila.

2706
01:48:18,300 --> 01:48:18,800
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Metro Manila.

2707
01:48:18,800 --> 01:48:19,860
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: National Capital Region.

2708
01:48:20,220 --> 01:48:26,360
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ang tataasan ng kanilang daily minimum.

2709
01:48:26,720 --> 01:48:27,380
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yes, yes po.

2710
01:48:27,540 --> 01:48:32,120
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At yun po ay pagtinuos natin sa loob ng isang buwan at ito ay 26 days,

2711
01:48:32,600 --> 01:48:36,320
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ay yun po ay 1,560 increase per month.

2712
01:48:36,900 --> 01:48:42,480
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At yung tanong nyo rin kanina para na-daplisan nyo ay patungkol sa ibang regyon,

2713
01:48:42,780 --> 01:48:46,320
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: effective October 14 sa Central Visayas,

2714
01:48:46,320 --> 01:48:49,780
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: si Bubuhol at sinama pa po yung dalawang bahagi.

2715
01:48:49,780 --> 01:48:56,020
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ngayon ang Negros Island Region, dahil hindi pa po buo yung wage board sa Negros Island Region,

2716
01:48:56,200 --> 01:48:58,660
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ito po yung Negros Oriental at si Quijor,

2717
01:48:59,040 --> 01:49:04,060
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ay magkakaroon sila ng karagdagang 42 pesos, effective October 14.

2718
01:49:04,500 --> 01:49:13,200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At sa loob ng isang buwan, yung mga kababayan natin sa Central Visayas ay makakatanggap ng 1,092 pesos monthly increase.

2719
01:49:13,200 --> 01:49:19,760
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ito po ay aabutin ng 385,000 minimum wage.

2720
01:49:19,780 --> 01:49:29,640
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So ito na yung mga nakatakdang wage increases sa ibang regyon, hindi lamang sa Metro Manila.

2721
01:49:31,120 --> 01:49:40,140
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Since ang wage setting is done through the respective regional tripartite wages and productivity boards.

2722
01:49:40,140 --> 01:49:45,260
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So pakiulit lang po, aside sa NCR, ano ang regyon po yun?

2723
01:49:45,320 --> 01:49:49,180
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Yung Region 7 at bahagi po ng NIR.

2724
01:49:49,780 --> 01:49:52,400
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: NIR, ay sa Negros.

2725
01:49:53,240 --> 01:49:58,540
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ito pong napipinto na, malapit-lapit na, nag-uusap na,

2726
01:49:59,080 --> 01:50:04,220
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ang alam ko po, hinug na hinug na, ay yung Calabarzon.

2727
01:50:05,280 --> 01:50:10,620
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Hindi ko lang po mabanggit pa kung ano yung halaga dahil hindi pa naman napapublished

2728
01:50:10,620 --> 01:50:15,740
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: at hindi pa nakukonfirm ng National Wages and Productivity Commission, Calabarzon po.

2729
01:50:15,740 --> 01:50:19,740
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At ang susunod na po dyan ay yung region 7.

2730
01:50:19,780 --> 01:50:23,460
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yung Dabao po, nauna po yun, yung second tranche.

2731
01:50:23,560 --> 01:50:27,060
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Nagkaroon na rin po sa Dabao nitong mga nakaraang buwan.

2732
01:50:27,200 --> 01:50:28,240
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So yung mean Dabao region?

2733
01:50:28,440 --> 01:50:31,700
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Dabao region po, region 11 po. Tapos na rin po yun.

2734
01:50:32,340 --> 01:50:34,780
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Tahimik lang po yun pinatupad yung second tranche.

2735
01:50:35,340 --> 01:50:38,520
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So tinatanong siguro ng iba, bakit iba't iba yung petsa?

2736
01:50:39,000 --> 01:50:42,120
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Iba't iba po kasi yung, Your Honor, yung anniversary dates.

2737
01:50:42,800 --> 01:50:45,620
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Pagdating po ng anniversary date, dun palang kumikilos po.

2738
01:50:45,620 --> 01:50:48,920
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Bago dumating yung anniversary date, 60 days before,

2739
01:50:49,780 --> 01:50:54,900
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: nagsisimula yung consultation sa employer sector, employees, public hearing.

2740
01:50:55,000 --> 01:50:56,620
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Dun palang gumagalaw po yun, Your Honor.

2741
01:50:57,200 --> 01:51:01,820
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Maraming salamat. Regardless of ano yung amount, mas alam nyo po yun.

2742
01:51:02,040 --> 01:51:07,680
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Dahil mas alam nyo yung presyo ng bilihin dun, yung cost of living sa areas

2743
01:51:07,680 --> 01:51:10,660
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: na inaaprobahan ng ating board.

2744
01:51:10,660 --> 01:51:15,820
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Pero sabi ko nga, bawat piso, bawat sentimo na pagdagdag sahod

2745
01:51:15,820 --> 01:51:19,240
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: sa ating mga ordinaryong manggagawa, ay malaking tulong po yun sa kanila.

2746
01:51:19,780 --> 01:51:22,960
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sana po patuloy nyo itong tututukan.

2747
01:51:24,020 --> 01:51:28,160
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At sabi ko nga kanina, sa mga malalaking negosyante,

2748
01:51:28,360 --> 01:51:31,260
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: kung hindi naman po, hindi nyo naman po ikakalugi,

2749
01:51:31,420 --> 01:51:33,520
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: hindi naman po malaking kawalan sa inyo,

2750
01:51:33,780 --> 01:51:37,580
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: sana i-share nyo na lang po ang bihaya sa inyong buhay

2751
01:51:37,580 --> 01:51:42,880
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: na makatulong po sa mga may hirap nating manggagawa.

2752
01:51:44,100 --> 01:51:46,400
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Salamat po. Sana patuloy nyo itong tututukan.

2753
01:51:48,160 --> 01:51:49,420
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Another topic lang po.

2754
01:51:49,780 --> 01:51:52,040
Senator Joel Villanueva: Can we go to another topic, Senator Bongo?

2755
01:51:52,060 --> 01:51:59,320
Senator Joel Villanueva: I think this is very crucial and a lot of people are waiting to discuss this particular issue.

2756
01:51:59,320 --> 01:52:07,800
Senator Joel Villanueva: And if I may butt in, first, we'd like to put on record that we indeed passed a resolution

2757
01:52:07,800 --> 01:52:16,680
Senator Joel Villanueva: here in the Senate calling for the implementation of the wage order NCR 27.

2758
01:52:17,820 --> 01:52:19,320
Senator Joel Villanueva: And then, of course...

2759
01:52:19,780 --> 01:52:24,380
Senator Joel Villanueva: Of course, we'd like to put on record that then Senator Francis Tolentino,

2760
01:52:24,620 --> 01:52:31,100
Senator Joel Villanueva: Senator Bongo and this representation worked together in passing the measure

2761
01:52:31,100 --> 01:52:35,400
Senator Joel Villanueva: that would give additional 100 peso increase for our workers.

2762
01:52:35,560 --> 01:52:41,300
Senator Joel Villanueva: We were able to pass it on third and final reading here in this institution in the Senate.

2763
01:52:41,300 --> 01:52:48,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: But unfortunately, it didn't reach the bicameral conference committee report.

2764
01:52:48,220 --> 01:52:50,300
Senator Joel Villanueva: For various reasons.

2765
01:52:50,600 --> 01:52:55,280
Senator Joel Villanueva: But let me just talk about this NCR order 27.

2766
01:52:55,560 --> 01:53:04,200
Senator Joel Villanueva: One, it's very clear in Article 126 of the Labor Code that the court should not

2767
01:53:04,200 --> 01:53:10,420
Senator Joel Villanueva: and will not in any way issue a temporary restraining order.

2768
01:53:10,420 --> 01:53:17,760
Senator Joel Villanueva: And yet, dito po sa Pasig RTC, nakapag-issue ng TRO.

2769
01:53:17,760 --> 01:53:20,860
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yan ang sitwasyon.

2770
01:53:21,000 --> 01:53:24,360
Senator Joel Villanueva: And then, nung ma-issue po yung TRO, dahil temporary nga po,

2771
01:53:24,840 --> 01:53:27,940
Senator Joel Villanueva: sabi din po doon sa interview doon sa clerk of court,

2772
01:53:28,320 --> 01:53:34,700
Senator Joel Villanueva: kung wala hong mabibigay na bond na amounting to 10 billion pesos,

2773
01:53:35,100 --> 01:53:38,380
Senator Joel Villanueva: hindi magkakaroon ng preliminary injunction.

2774
01:53:38,660 --> 01:53:44,500
Senator Joel Villanueva: But unfortunately, ngayon, correct me if I'm wrong, again, just to put the record straight,

2775
01:53:44,900 --> 01:53:46,640
Senator Joel Villanueva: may preliminary injunction.

2776
01:53:46,640 --> 01:53:46,800
Senator Joel Villanueva: Okay.

2777
01:53:47,760 --> 01:53:57,760
Senator Joel Villanueva: Nagkaroon ng preliminary injunction, ang DOLE issued naman itong NCR 28, Wage Order 28.

2778
01:53:59,880 --> 01:54:07,400
Senator Joel Villanueva: Now, in effect, while NCR 27 remains under litigation.

2779
01:54:07,400 --> 01:54:16,900
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, yung question po dito, what is DOLE's legal position on the additional 25 pesos,

2780
01:54:16,900 --> 01:54:21,400
Senator Joel Villanueva: second tranche, under the NCR 27?

2781
01:54:22,080 --> 01:54:29,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: Now, it's supposed to be scheduled on January of 2027, next year, no?

2782
01:54:29,960 --> 01:54:32,060
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kasi yun yung mga questions po eh.

2783
01:54:32,300 --> 01:54:38,680
Senator Joel Villanueva: Kung yung NCR Wage Order 27 ay ultimately ma-upheld,

2784
01:54:40,320 --> 01:54:42,180
Senator Joel Villanueva: yung tinatanong kayo ng Senator Bong,

2785
01:54:42,180 --> 01:54:46,380
Senator Joel Villanueva: will the 25 pesos, second tranche, remain?

2786
01:54:46,900 --> 01:54:58,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: Payable in addition to the 60 pesos rate presently implemented under itong bagong NCR Wage Order 28?

2787
01:54:58,120 --> 01:55:11,660
Senator Joel Villanueva: Or, does DOLE consider NCR 28 to have somehow superseded or otherwise affected NCR Wage Order 27?

2788
01:55:12,280 --> 01:55:15,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang magandaw dito sa Senado, napag-uusapan ang gusto.

2789
01:55:15,220 --> 01:55:19,440
Senator Joel Villanueva: Hindi pa sigawan tayo dito, hindi pa taasa ng boses.

2790
01:55:19,640 --> 01:55:26,300
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mas gusto namin maintindihan yung ating posisyon dahil kahit magkaiba ho yung maging posisyon po natin,

2791
01:55:26,380 --> 01:55:28,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: we will respect each other's position.

2792
01:55:29,000 --> 01:55:30,080
Senator Joel Villanueva: Secretary Tolentino, please.

2793
01:55:30,480 --> 01:55:36,140
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Salamat po. Medyo masalimut nga po yung katanungan yun at kung ano yung magiging resulta.

2794
01:55:36,260 --> 01:55:43,560
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kaya kanina pa ho, sinabi ko na yung fate, yung kahinat na ng Wage Order 27

2795
01:55:43,560 --> 01:55:46,180
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ay ibinibigay na po natin sa husgado.

2796
01:55:46,940 --> 01:55:51,520
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kung sinabi po ng husgado, ganito, ganito, ganito, yun po yung ating susundin.

2797
01:55:51,520 --> 01:55:56,420
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Dalawa po yung ating ginawa dito sa pag-issue ng Wage Order 28.

2798
01:55:56,860 --> 01:56:04,220
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ginalang po natin, nirespeto po natin, yumuko po tayo sa mandato ng husgado.

2799
01:56:04,400 --> 01:56:13,020
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: We respected the two RTCs, the two Supreme Court cases filed, and even the Supreme Court na pinakamataas na hukuman.

2800
01:56:13,020 --> 01:56:16,020
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Na pending pa rin ngayon. Ginalang po natin sila.

2801
01:56:16,660 --> 01:56:18,000
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Hinihintay natin kung...

2802
01:56:18,000 --> 01:56:19,140
Senator Joel Villanueva: Despite our disagreement.

2803
01:56:19,420 --> 01:56:20,160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yes, opo.

2804
01:56:20,360 --> 01:56:20,680
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Thank you.

2805
01:56:21,040 --> 01:56:25,520
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yung nakalagay sa Article 126.

2806
01:56:25,640 --> 01:56:31,420
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kasi ang sabi nila, pag wala daw pong ban, ay dapat ay hindi na dapat igalang.

2807
01:56:31,920 --> 01:56:41,200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang sa atin po dito, may mga desisyon ng Supreme Court, kahit po walang ban, dapat ang husgado rin na magsabi na walang ban, dapat ito ay patupad nyo na.

2808
01:56:41,200 --> 01:56:47,280
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So balit hinintay po natin, hinintay po natin lahat, at ginalang natin.

2809
01:56:47,380 --> 01:56:49,800
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So balit, ipinaglaban po natin.

2810
01:56:50,380 --> 01:56:58,260
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ipinaglalaban po natin, in fact po, Your Honor, sa October 2, ay deadline namin para sumagot po sa RTC na botas.

2811
01:56:59,000 --> 01:57:02,400
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang sasagot po nito ay ang Office of Solicitor General.

2812
01:57:02,720 --> 01:57:10,180
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Doon po sa Supreme Court, ang alam ko po ay humingi pa ng ilang days ang Office of the Solicitor General para tumugon.

2813
01:57:10,180 --> 01:57:11,900
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Para mag-file ng comment.

2814
01:57:12,440 --> 01:57:20,700
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yung dalawang kaso po sa Court of Appeals ay hindi pa po pinapakomment ang Office of the Solicitor General.

2815
01:57:21,300 --> 01:57:30,860
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Si RTC 152, dahil kami nag-file ng, pinagpatuloy po namin ipaglaban nito, nag-file kami ng motion for reconsideration,

2816
01:57:31,680 --> 01:57:37,180
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: may narapat po ng 152 nung nag-file sa...

2817
01:57:39,240 --> 01:57:40,180
Senator Joel Villanueva: Before you continue.

2818
01:57:40,180 --> 01:57:46,520
Senator Joel Villanueva: Before you continue, Secretary Tolentino, another former colleague of yours misses you, so he's here.

2819
01:57:47,000 --> 01:57:51,780
Senator Joel Villanueva: And he's now the chairperson of the Senate Committee on Finance, Senator J.V. Ejercito.

2820
01:57:52,100 --> 01:57:58,900
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pwede ko kayong pumalakpak kung gusto niyong magkaroon ng pagbabago itong malaking binawas sa DOLE.

2821
01:57:59,200 --> 01:58:00,880
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, Secretary Tolentino, please continue.

2822
01:58:01,940 --> 01:58:04,180
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Medyo nawala po ako dahil sa pag...

2823
01:58:04,820 --> 01:58:08,180
Senator Joel Villanueva: You're on the part yung sa CA and the court orders.

2824
01:58:08,180 --> 01:58:09,500
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yes, I'm on the part of the court orders.

2825
01:58:10,180 --> 01:58:15,120
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Pagdating po ng paggalang sa pagdating kay Senator J.V., nakakalimutan ko na yung sasabihin ko.

2826
01:58:15,660 --> 01:58:22,060
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So yung dalawa pong Court of Appeals ay nakapending at hindi pa po kami pinapakomment.

2827
01:58:22,520 --> 01:58:33,420
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yung 152 po, dahil pinaglaban natin yung 27, nag-file po ang Office of the Solicitor General ng motion for reconsideration kasama po ang DOLE.

2828
01:58:35,060 --> 01:58:39,420
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Subalit, subalit, ang tingin ng husgado, yung lingwahe ng motion for reconsideration,

2829
01:58:40,180 --> 01:58:43,060
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ay masakit.

2830
01:58:43,840 --> 01:58:47,920
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kaya kami ngayon ay pinasasagot bakit hindi raw kami makukontempt.

2831
01:58:48,380 --> 01:58:50,340
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Why we should not be cited for contempt.

2832
01:58:50,520 --> 01:58:53,980
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang deadline po nito ay ito rin atang 1st week of October.

2833
01:58:54,600 --> 01:59:00,500
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ito po ay nagpapatuna, Your Honor, na patuloy po natin pinaglalaban ang Wage Order 27.

2834
01:59:01,340 --> 01:59:03,640
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At ang dami po namin kaso nang inaabot dito.

2835
01:59:03,640 --> 01:59:10,160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kaya sa haba po ng mga kaso at dokumento, hindi naman po makakahintay ang ating mga manggagawa.

2836
01:59:10,220 --> 01:59:11,800
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Dahil ganito po yun.

2837
01:59:11,980 --> 01:59:22,380
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Dapat po, by October, bago pumasok ang November, yung mga HR departments ay hinahanda na po yung 13-month pay at Christmas bonus computations.

2838
01:59:23,060 --> 01:59:27,520
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kaya nga po yung Wage Order 28 ay yung po ay nakaabang para dito.

2839
01:59:28,020 --> 01:59:33,500
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Para makasama na kung sino yung mabibigyan ng prorated Christmas bonus, 13-month pay.

2840
01:59:33,500 --> 01:59:37,700
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At ganon din po sa mga holidays na parating.

2841
01:59:38,180 --> 01:59:39,500
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kagaya po nitong Ascension.

2842
01:59:40,180 --> 01:59:44,400
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kaya yung holidays natin, ilang araw po tayo walang pasok dito sa Metro Manila.

2843
01:59:44,900 --> 01:59:49,020
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yung ating 60 pesos ay kasama na rin po doon sa holiday computation.

2844
01:59:49,820 --> 01:59:53,880
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ganon din po sa night shift differential, overtime pay, etc., etc.

2845
01:59:54,340 --> 02:00:00,020
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: I would like to reiterate, Your Honor, patuloy po pinaglalaban ang Office of the Solicitor General ang Wage Order 27.

2846
02:00:00,000 --> 02:00:09,040
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kung ano po ang kahinatnan po nito, hindi po natin alam dahil limang husgado po ang mihawak.

2847
02:00:09,460 --> 02:00:11,840
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kaya mahalaga po ang Wage Order 28.

2848
02:00:12,280 --> 02:00:19,440
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Habang ipinagtatanggol ang Wage Order 27, ay hindi po makakahintay ang ating mga manggagawa.

2849
02:00:19,440 --> 02:00:30,240
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Na sinabi po, naniniwala po ako sa sinabi ni Sen. Bongo na mahalaga ang bawat piso, yung agarampong 60 pesos, bawat araw ay isang relief para sa ating manggagawa.

2850
02:00:30,300 --> 02:01:01,600
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you very much for that, because this would clear the air, especially between this representation and the Secretary of DOLE, because I was quoted one time that I was and the Secretary of DOLE, that we have two different opinions. And it's good to note that we are not giving up NCR 27. We are still fighting for it and we might have different views on how to fight it out.

2851
02:01:02,020 --> 02:01:11,300
Senator Joel Villanueva: But let me ask, if NCR 27 is again ultimately upheld, what would happen to the 25 pesos second tranche?

2852
02:01:11,560 --> 02:01:21,860
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mag-remain po ba itong payable in addition dun sa 60 pesos rate being implemented now in the NCR Wage Order 28?

2853
02:01:22,540 --> 02:01:44,700
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Salamat po. Uulitin ko po kung ano po ang kahihinatnan ng Wage Order 27. Kung ano po ang ilalabas na bahagi ng desisyon, kung ito po ay Navotas, kung ito po ay Pasig, kung ito po ay Court of Appeals, kung ito po ay Supreme Court, tayo po ay tatalima dito, kung ano po yung sasabihin.

2854
02:01:44,700 --> 02:01:47,020
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you for that. I understand that fully.

2855
02:01:47,020 --> 02:01:49,020
Senator Joel Villanueva: It's just that one thing that bothers me...

2856
02:01:49,440 --> 02:01:58,540
Senator Joel Villanueva: is the fact that the Wage Boards is not supposed to issue another round of increase in a year, in a year's time.

2857
02:01:58,860 --> 02:02:03,580
Senator Joel Villanueva: Will it be? I'm not a legal expert here. The Secretary of Labor is.

2858
02:02:03,580 --> 02:02:17,800
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I was just wondering, hindi ba makaka-apekto yun dun sa ating patuloy na pakikibaka para ma-implement itong Wage Order No. 27?

2859
02:02:19,440 --> 02:02:31,880
Senator Joel Villanueva: Na maaaring nag-supersed na itong Wage Order No. 28 at hindi na natin ito kailangang pagtuunan ng pansin yung Wage Order No. 27

2860
02:02:31,880 --> 02:02:40,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: dahil isang beses lamang po pwedeng mag-increase ang Wage Board tungkol dito sa usapin na ito, Secretary.

2861
02:02:40,560 --> 02:02:49,000
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Siguro po for the record, ulitin ko po, Wage Order No. 28 is a separate...

2862
02:02:49,440 --> 02:02:52,000
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: and independent wage relief.

2863
02:02:53,800 --> 02:03:01,680
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Wage Order No. 27 remains defended in pending judicial proceedings.

2864
02:03:01,680 --> 02:03:11,000
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Wage Order No. 28 does not fully adjudicate whatever rights or legal consequences may arise under No. 27.

2865
02:03:11,000 --> 02:03:18,560
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Doli's core position remains, respect the courts, preserve No. 27, and deliver No. 28 now.

2866
02:03:18,560 --> 02:03:26,600
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So yung pong nakalagay sa batas na medyo komplikado na within one year, hindi po nag-apply yung within one year sa No. 28

2867
02:03:26,600 --> 02:03:32,160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: kasi hindi po na-implement si No. 27. Pinatay na po ito one day before.

2868
02:03:32,740 --> 02:03:37,880
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Nagsimula po si No. 28 sa No. 26 na umiiral noong nakaraan linggo.

2869
02:03:38,580 --> 02:03:47,240
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So lahat po ng mawalanggalang na, lahat po ng usapin patungkol sa No. 27 ay nakasalalay na po iyan sa husgado.

2870
02:03:47,240 --> 02:03:48,540
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kung sabihin ang husgado,

2871
02:03:48,560 --> 02:03:52,300
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ibigay niyo si No. 25 next year, susundin po iyon.

2872
02:03:53,000 --> 02:03:56,900
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kung sabihin ang husgado na ganito, hindi natin mapangunahan.

2873
02:03:57,140 --> 02:04:01,980
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang amin lang pong sinaalang-alang ay dahil nakapasok sa Supreme Court,

2874
02:04:02,800 --> 02:04:04,620
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ay may katagalan po talaga sa...

2875
02:04:04,620 --> 02:04:12,360
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Huwag naman magalit sa atin na ang Supreme Court, may katagalan po talaga pag nakarating sa kataas-taas sa hukuman.

2876
02:04:12,360 --> 02:04:18,540
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At baka hindi po umabot sa 13-month pay o sa Christmas bonus na kailangan-kailangan,

2877
02:04:18,560 --> 02:04:23,140
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ng ating mga manggagawa, lalo na ngayong darating na kapaskuhan.

2878
02:04:23,700 --> 02:04:27,140
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you, thank you, Secretary. That clears a lot of things.

2879
02:04:27,720 --> 02:04:35,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: And now that NCR 28 is in effect, perhaps, yun talaga ngayon yung question,

2880
02:04:35,280 --> 02:04:45,940
Senator Joel Villanueva: how did Department of Labor and Employment ensure full and uniform compliance with the new wage rates

2881
02:04:45,940 --> 02:04:51,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: beyond enforcing the statutory minimum?

2882
02:04:51,000 --> 02:05:04,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang dole po ba maintain a regularly updated regional benchmark for the income required to meet po yung basic household needs?

2883
02:05:04,460 --> 02:05:14,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: And can this be transparently compared with the prevailing minimum wages during wage board deliberations?

2884
02:05:14,000 --> 02:05:15,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sir?

2885
02:05:15,000 --> 02:05:21,060
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Dumaan po ito sa masusing proseso ng wage boards, yung consultations,

2886
02:05:21,260 --> 02:05:26,120
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ganun din po sa National Wages and Productivity Council.

2887
02:05:26,760 --> 02:05:33,800
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang score nga po doon sa National Wages and Productivity Council, if I'm not mistaken, is 5-1.

2888
02:05:37,760 --> 02:05:42,140
Senator Joel Villanueva: I will leave the floor to my chairman, Chairman J.V., please.

2889
02:05:42,140 --> 02:05:42,680
Senator Joel Villanueva: Please.

2890
02:05:42,680 --> 02:05:48,520
Senator Joel Villanueva: Who will also sponsor the resolution for the JIL anniversary.

2891
02:05:48,800 --> 02:05:49,100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

2892
02:05:49,520 --> 02:05:52,140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Our chair, our vice chair, Sir Joel.

2893
02:05:52,760 --> 02:05:55,600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Good afternoon sa ating dole family.

2894
02:05:55,860 --> 02:06:02,000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Of course, led by our former colleague and hardworking secretary, Francis Tolentino,

2895
02:06:02,180 --> 02:06:04,560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to the USECs, ASECs, and the different ends of agencies.

2896
02:06:04,720 --> 02:06:05,280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Magandang hapon.

2897
02:06:06,000 --> 02:06:12,380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Anyway, siyempre, biglang chairman ng Committee of Finance, I will napansin ko lang may mga, of course, as always,

2898
02:06:12,380 --> 02:06:21,180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: because of our fiscal space, medyo karamihan ng departments and agencies received considerable cuts.

2899
02:06:21,480 --> 02:06:23,680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Medyo malaki po yung sa dole.

2900
02:06:26,000 --> 02:06:27,320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Parang 14 billion.

2901
02:06:28,000 --> 02:06:31,580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, just a basic question.

2902
02:06:31,820 --> 02:06:36,340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi, I will deliver a sponsorship speech lang.

2903
02:06:36,340 --> 02:06:38,340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I'll try to be back right away.

2904
02:06:38,540 --> 02:06:41,340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yun tungkol sa JICA and also...

2905
02:06:42,380 --> 02:06:45,520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Well, JIL anniversary and JICA, no?

2906
02:06:45,940 --> 02:06:47,020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Accommodation for JICA.

2907
02:06:47,180 --> 02:06:50,920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But anyway, siguro, basic questions are later, no?

2908
02:06:51,000 --> 02:06:53,460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ano yung mga affected programs, as always.

2909
02:06:54,320 --> 02:06:55,140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We'll do our best.

2910
02:06:56,340 --> 02:06:58,280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ano naman to, zero-sum kasi talaga.

2911
02:06:58,460 --> 02:07:02,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, if we need to add, we need to subtract.

2912
02:07:02,860 --> 02:07:06,360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We will have to deduct from other programs, no?

2913
02:07:06,360 --> 02:07:08,060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pero, yun lang.

2914
02:07:08,540 --> 02:07:12,360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro, gusto natin malaman kung ano yung mga affected programs.

2915
02:07:12,380 --> 02:07:15,660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Anyway, ito po, less than 14 billion.

2916
02:07:16,480 --> 02:07:19,640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro, sa house, will be a little bit bigger, I'm sure.

2917
02:07:20,000 --> 02:07:21,700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I'm sure they will also add.

2918
02:07:22,200 --> 02:07:25,060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Asek, meron na bang ano ang house sa HCAP?

2919
02:07:26,820 --> 02:07:27,680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Meron na bang ano?

2920
02:07:27,760 --> 02:07:28,500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Meron na ba tayong copy?

2921
02:07:28,720 --> 02:07:36,600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How much did they amend to increase?

2922
02:07:37,340 --> 02:07:40,060
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Wala pa po kaming copy, Your Honor.

2923
02:07:40,060 --> 02:07:42,360
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Pero, alam ko, nag-meeting na sila.

2924
02:07:42,380 --> 02:07:45,300
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Hindi pa namin hawak yung kopya.

2925
02:07:45,300 --> 02:07:49,300
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Pero, naniniwala po kayo, honor, na hindi naman nyo kami pababayaan.

2926
02:07:52,200 --> 02:07:54,260
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Of course, we'll do our best.

2927
02:07:54,340 --> 02:07:58,040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi problema lang ng problema ngayon, as compared to last year.

2928
02:07:58,760 --> 02:08:03,440
